#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# divisor_sigma

#% text
# `divisor_sigma(k, n)` gives the sum of the `k`-th powers of the positive divisors of `n`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `divisor_sigma(0, n)` counts the divisors, `divisor_sigma(1, n)` adds them. It is computed from the factorisation of `n`.

#% item
# `divisor_sigma` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
divisor_sigma(1, 12)
#% output
#= 28

#% cell
divisor_sigma(0, 12)
#% output
#= 6

#% cell
divisor_sigma(2, 10)
#% output
#= 130

#% cell
divisor_sigma(1, range(10))
#% output
#= [1, 3, 4, 7, 6, 12, 8, 15, 13, 18]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A large argument:

#% cell
divisor_sigma(1, 10^18)
#% output
#= 2499995231628286897

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The same as adding powers of the divisors:

#% cell
[divisor_sigma(3, 28), sum(divisors(28)^3)]
#% output
#= [25112, 25112]

#% text
# `divisor_sigma(1, n) = 2n` for a perfect number:

#% cell
divisor_sigma(1, 8128) - 2*8128
#% output
#= 0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `divisors`, `divisor_sum`, `euler_phi`
